scued  us from the classic door jamb situation  when we were trying for the fifth time  to rescue the skirmisher from prison  these bonds run so deep that if a  significant other dies the surviving  squad mate will go berserk for a brief  period of time  number four photo finish the photo booth  is a bit cheesy but what photo booth  isn't the wealth of customization  options from backgrounds to poses can  result in stylized images that border on  brand-building  at least your dynamic duo's will be  ready for their personality driven  businesses after the war it's a nice  light-hearted touch in the middle of a  very serious campaign number five the  chosen are persistent and grow each  chosen enemy will set up somewhere in  the world and begin to harass players  and their harassment have practical  benefits every time they kidnap or  subdue one of your soldiers they extract  knowledge and information these make the  chosen stronger and more skilled the  next time you see them in other words  their reoccurring bosses who grow over  time each has a different fighting style  for example the assassin will  immediately try and incapacitate and  interrogate your soldiers while the  hunter will mark targets at range who  must get to cover or be instantly Kayode  we were told the assassin will actually  adapt her fighting style based on the  tactical decisions you make in previous  engagements  no one has ever done that paper no one  shall ever do that again  number six loot the chosen hunter  warlock and assassin have some pretty  sweet gear like a sniper rifle  sword and whatever warlocks have mined  bullets if you successfully kill one of  them you get to keep their epic weapon  and use it against their coworkers  hopefully that will play a role in your  decision-making process over which one  to go after first assuming you get that  option and number 7 okay they're called  the lost but they're really zombies the  lost are equal-opportunity brain eaters  and they'll go after XCOM soldiers or  Advent alike they are attracted by noise  especially large explosions in the lost  and abandoned mission we played there  weren't so much of a threat on their own  since killing one guarantees another  action but we could see them becoming a  real problem when added on top of  already harrowing fights with the Advent  how is the war of the chose an expansion  looking to you is this what you want for  your next Ironman run or are there other  features you've been hotly requesting  from the devs let us know in the  comments below and check out our  gameplay on the lost and abandoned  mission thanks for watching  [Music]
 

